{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-027",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 27,
  "title": "Job 27",
  "display_title": "Job 27",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 27,
  "sortOrder": 18027,
  "verseCount": 23,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Moreover Job continued his parable, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "As God liveth, who hath taken away my judgment; and the Almighty, who hath vexed my soul;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "All the while my breath is in me, and the spirit of God is in my nostrils;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "My lips shall not speak wickedness, nor my tongue utter deceit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "God forbid that I should justify you: till I die I will not remove mine integrity from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "My righteousness I hold fast, and will not let it go: my heart shall not reproach me so long as I live.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Let mine enemy be as the wicked, and he that riseth up against me as the unrighteous.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For what is the hope of the hypocrite, though he hath gained, when God taketh away his soul?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Will God hear his cry when trouble cometh upon him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Will he delight himself in the Almighty? will he always call upon God?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "I will teach you by the hand of God: that which is with the Almighty will I not conceal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Behold, all ye yourselves have seen it; why then are ye thus altogether vain?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "This is the portion of a wicked man with God, and the heritage of oppressors, which they shall receive of the Almighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "If his children be multiplied, it is for the sword: and his offspring shall not be satisfied with bread.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Those that remain of him shall be buried in death: and his widows shall not weep.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Though he heap up silver as the dust, and prepare raiment as the clay;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "He may prepare it, but the just shall put it on, and the innocent shall divide the silver.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He buildeth his house as a moth, and as a booth that the keeper maketh.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The rich man shall lie down, but he shall not be gathered: he openeth his eyes, and he is not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Terrors take hold on him as waters, a tempest stealeth him away in the night.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "The east wind carrieth him away, and he departeth: and as a storm hurleth him out of his place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For God shall cast upon him, and not spare: he would fain flee out of his hand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:27:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Men shall clap their hands at him, and shall hiss him out of his place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 27:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:27:23"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
